| `shell.formatter` | string | `shfmt` | an adapter name `scripts/shell_gate.py` has: `shfmt` | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.formatter` row | Names the formatter `make fmt-check-sh` runs to report a difference and `make fmt-sh` runs to rewrite the files. A name with no adapter is exit 14 before anything runs, because the flags are the tool's own; the tool on neither the interpreter's directory nor PATH is exit 11 naming it. Absent, the targets write `[using default] shell.formatter = "shfmt"` to stderr. | the linter: `shell.linter` | always |
